## Phase 3 — Restaurant Onboarding and Menu Management

### Goal
Let restaurant owners create restaurants and manage menus.

- [ ] **Create restaurant creation endpoint.**
  - Route: `POST /api/v1/restaurants`.
  - Allowed role: RESTAURANT or ADMIN.
  - Save:
    - name
    - description
    - lat/lng
    - delivery radius
    - prep time

- [ ] **Convert lat/lng to PostGIS point.**
  - Store as SRID 4326.
  - Validate coordinate range.

- [ ] **Create restaurant update endpoint.**
  - Route: `PATCH /api/v1/restaurants/{id}`.
  - Ensure owner can edit only their restaurant.

- [ ] **Create activate/deactivate restaurant endpoint.**
  - Toggle `is_active`.
  - Inactive restaurants should not appear in search.

- [ ] **Create open/close restaurant endpoint.**
  - Toggle `is_open`.
  - Closed restaurants cannot accept orders.

- [ ] **Create menu item creation endpoint.**
  - Route: `POST /api/v1/menu-items`.
  - Validate restaurant ownership.
  - Store price as Decimal.

- [ ] **Create menu item update endpoint.**
  - Route: `PATCH /api/v1/menu-items/{id}`.
  - Allow price/name/description update.

- [ ] **Create menu availability toggle.**
  - Route: `PATCH /api/v1/menu-items/{id}/availability`.
  - Use this for out-of-stock items.

- [ ] **Create restaurant detail endpoint.**
  - Route: `GET /api/v1/restaurants/{id}`.
  - Include:
    - restaurant info
    - open status
    - menu items

- [ ] **Create restaurant menu endpoint.**
  - Route: `GET /api/v1/restaurants/{id}/menu`.
  - Only show available items to customers.

- [ ] **Add pagination for restaurant lists.**
  - Use limit/offset or cursor pagination.

- [ ] **Add authorization checks.**
  - Restaurant owner cannot edit another restaurant.
  - Admin can override.

- [ ] **Add restaurant tests.**
  - Create restaurant.
  - Update menu.
  - Unauthorized access.
  - Closed restaurant behavior.

### Done when:
A restaurant owner can onboard, create menu items, and customers can view restaurant/menu data.

