## Phase 18 — Security Hardening

### Goal
Protect user data and platform integrity.

- [ ] **Use HTTPS everywhere.**
  - TLS termination at Nginx/Traefik.
  - Redirect HTTP to HTTPS.

- [ ] **Hash passwords strongly.**
  - Argon2 recommended.
  - No MD5/SHA1.

- [ ] **Use short-lived access tokens.**
  - Example:
    - access token: 15–30 minutes
    - refresh token: longer with rotation

- [ ] **Add rate limiting.**
  - Protect:
    - login
    - register
    - checkout
    - webhook
    - WebSocket connect

- [ ] **Validate all input.**
  - Use Pydantic schemas.
  - Reject unknown fields if needed.

- [ ] **Protect webhooks.**
  - Signature verification.
  - Replay protection.
  - IP allowlist if provider supports.

- [ ] **Use CORS carefully.**
  - Allow known frontend origins only.

- [ ] **Add RBAC checks on every protected endpoint.**
  - Never trust frontend role alone.

- [ ] **Prevent IDOR attacks.**
  - User can access only their own orders.
  - Restaurant can access only their own resources.
  - Driver can access only assigned orders.

- [ ] **Store secrets securely.**
  - No secrets in code.
  - Use secret manager in production.

- [ ] **Add SQL safety.**
  - Use ORM/query builder.
  - Avoid raw string interpolation.

- [ ] **Add WebSocket authorization.**
  - Authenticate before subscribing.
  - Validate resource ownership.

### Done when:
The backend has basic production-grade authentication, authorization, rate limiting, and secret hygiene.

